{"step_index":2815,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T13:22:05Z","input_tokens":2793,"cache_read_tokens":74053,"output_tokens":2287,"thinking":"The interface provides a comprehensive view of the execution process, correlating code, iterations, and memory state. This integrated display facilitates pinpointing the source of errors. The clear visual organization suggests a methodical debugging approach.\n\n\nAnalyzing requirements for Phase 9, starting with visual consistency. Ensuring the DSA section adheres to the established aesthetic: light cards, borders, shadows, and fonts. Will standardize spacing throughout the DSA interface for a more compact and balanced appearance.\n\nFocused on typography, adjusting font weights for headers, titles, tags, and descriptions to improve readability. Implementing line height and color adjustments for primary and supporting text. Plan to style code blocks with a monospace font and subtle background for better contrast and clarity.\n\nAddressing navigation by implementing a unified breadcrumb trail. Defining specific breadcrumb paths for the dashboard and topics, with further considerations for problem navigation.\n\n\nDefining specific navigation affordances for DSA sections and workspaces. Implementing \"Previous/Next Problem\" controls directly within the workspace header, alongside back buttons for quick navigation to catalogs and the dashboard. Considering appropriate mobile responsiveness by adapting the layout of tables and metrics on smaller screens.\n\n\nDeveloping clear visual feedback for various states, starting with empty states for filters, notes, bookmarks, and reviews, providing informative messages and actions. Implementing visual cues for loading states during code execution and testing. Creating user-friendly error messages, including syntax and test failure cases, with hints.\nAdding high-contrast badges to indicate the status of problems (solved, attempted, bookmarked, review).\n\n\nImplementing a consistent visual language for problem statuses using distinct pill colors and a gold star for bookmarks. Ensuring the placement of these indicators remains uniform across the application.\n\nPrioritizing a clean user interface by avoiding excessive dashboards and animations, opting for a structured, calm design with crisp transitions that respect user preferences for reduced motion. Data accuracy is a priority, generating statistics from actual progress data, avoiding misleading metrics or gamification elements.\n\nDeveloping a \"Beginner Friendly Mode\" to simplify the interface, hiding technical metadata and presenting Big-O complexities in plain language, thus improving user comprehension. Detailed Mode is available for users needing raw complexity data.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"powershell -Command \\\"Select-String -Path 'C:\\\\Users\\\\CVT\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\code-flow-visualizer\\\\app_build\\\\styles.css' -Pattern 'dsa-learning-container' -Context 0,20\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CVT\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\code-flow-visualizer\\\\app_build\"","IsDaemon":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Finding dsa-learning-container in styles.css\"","toolSummary":"\"Find dsa-learning-container in styles.css\""}}]}
